jobs.prompt:
Acceptance review (read-only; do not edit any file) of tickets built in PR A on branch swarm/s4s5-a. For each ticket below, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met by the implementation, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read the files; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-0160", "title": "E2e harness cleans up local test data after each run", "files": ["tools/e2e-data-cleanup.mjs"], "acceptance": ["E2e runs clean up their own local test data, and a local-only cleanup tool refuses non-localhost databases."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0161", "title": "Local-only test database cleanup refuses non-localhost targets", "files": ["tools/test-db-cleanup.mjs"], "acceptance": ["A cleanup command exits with an error when the database URL host is not localhost."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0162", "title": "CI workflow template caches or mirrors Docker Hub images", "files": ["templates/coordination/ci-docker-hub-mirror.yml", "tools/ci-image-cache.mjs"], "acceptance": ["CI caches or mirrors images so Docker Hub rate limits don't fail runs."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0168", "title": "Turn each new failure cause into a regression test stub", "files": ["tools/failure-regression.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Each new failure cause becomes a regression test, and lane pass rates feed routing."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8001", "title": "Board worktree rows show their own ledger numbers or roll into the parent", "files": ["tools/board-data.mjs", "tools/watch-assets/board.js"], "acceptance": ["A worktree row shows per-branch numbers read from that worktree's own ledger, or worktrees roll into the parent row behind an \"N worktrees\" expander; it never copies the parent's percent, open or blocked counts.", "Test: a parent and a worktree with different ledgers show different numbers."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8002", "title": "Off-ledger run counts exclude smoke, lane-test and probe runs and link to a list", "files": ["tools/build-progress.mjs", "tools/watch-assets/project.js", "tools/watch-assets/board.js"], "acceptance": ["Runs whose manifest or job ids are smoke, lane-test or probe, and runs flagged nonIntegrating, are excluded from the off-ledger and untracked counts.", "The remaining count links to a list page of those runs.", "Test: smoke and probe runs excluded; a real manifest run counted and listed."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8003", "title": "Acceptance reviews work from any worktree of the repo", "files": ["tools/acceptance.mjs", "tools/scope-loop.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Acceptance-review manifests are generated for tickets built in a linked worktree: the ledger, run records and ticket files are resolved from the ticket's target worktree, not only the main checkout.", "Test: from a linked worktree, a review manifest is generated with that worktree's files."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8004", "title": "Tickets and stages carry an optional targetWorktree; dispatch, verify and review run there", "files": ["tools/tickets.mjs", "tools/scope-loop.mjs"], "acceptance": ["The ledger schema accepts an optional targetWorktree (path or branch) on a ticket and on a stage; validateTicket checks it.", "scope-loop dispatch, verify and acceptance review run in that worktree.", "Test: two stages on two worktrees run at once with no cross-writes."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-s4s5-a.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test. Be strict and concrete.
